/target/
/result
/result-*
crates/*/target/
crates/schematic-viewer/target/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.tmp
*.bak
# Transaction journals, active and abandoned; .konnect- from earlier releases.
.copperpour-transaction-*.json
.konnect-transaction-*.json
dist/

# Python bytecode. The plugin and packaging scripts are Python; running
# them (or the plugin tests) writes caches next to the sources, and three
# .pyc files had been committed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Files KiCad writes beside any board it opens. Running the live IPC suite
# means opening a board in KiCad, so every reviewer who does grows a set of
# these, and `git add -A` will otherwise sweep them in — a `.history/` gitlink
# and a lock file naming the developer's host and username both reached a
# commit that way.
#
#   .history/     KiCad 10 Local History: an embedded git repo of automatic
#                 snapshots, per-machine (Preferences > Common > Project Backup)
#   *.lck         transient board lock; contains {hostname, username}
#   *.kicad_prl   per-user local project settings, never shared
#   *.kicad_pro   generated on open for a bare .kicad_pcb fixture
#
# .kicad_pro takes three layers, because "generated" and "intentional" are
# both real and are distinguishable by name:
#
#   1. ignored everywhere by default — it is usually a machine dropping;
#   2. re-opened under tests/fixtures — the netclass tools (create_netclass,
#      assign_net_to_class) write to the sibling project file by design, so a
#      fixture exercising them needs one tracked on purpose, and a blanket
#      ignore would make `git add` skip it in silence: the same failure this
#      block exists to prevent, only inverted;
#   3. re-closed by name for the projects KiCad auto-generates beside the
#      tracked bare-board fixtures. Those names are predictable — KiCad writes
#      <board>.kicad_pro next to any bare <board>.kicad_pcb it opens — and
#      those exact files are always droppings, never intentional.
#
# So an intentional project fixture just needs a name of its own
# (netclass.kicad_pro, say) and is trackable with no edit here at all.
#
# .history/, *.lck and *.kicad_prl stay ignored everywhere, fixtures included:
# those must never be tracked even deliberately.
.history/
*.lck
*.kicad_prl
*.kicad_pro
!crates/*/tests/fixtures/*.kicad_pro
# Auto-generated beside the tracked bare boards (git ls-files '*.kicad_pcb').
# Order matters: last match wins, so these must follow the negation.
crates/copperpour-ipc/tests/fixtures/live_ipc.kicad_pro
crates/copperpour-core/tests/fixtures/test.kicad_pro
